{
  "title": "ISic001293. Funerary inscription",
  "body": "<div id=\"editions\"><div class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Jonathan Prag</div><div id=\"edition-interpretive\" lang=\"grc\">  <div class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\"><span class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  <a id=\"al1-interpretive\"><!--0--></a><span class=\"linenumber\">1</span><span data-text=\"Θεοῖς\">Θ(εοῖς)</span>  <span data-text=\"Καταχθονίοις\">Κ(αταχθονίοις)</span>  <br id=\"al2-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">2</span><span data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Δάφνη\"><span data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Δάφνη\">Δάφνη</span></span>  <span data-text=\"γλυκυ\n                    τάτη\">γλυ[κυ-]<br id=\"al3-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">3</span>τάτη</span>  <span data-text=\"χαῖρε\">χαῖρ[ε]</span>  <span data-text=\"ἔζη\n                    σας\">[ἔζη-]<br id=\"al4-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">4</span>σας</span>  <span data-text=\"ἔτη\">ἔτη</span> [<span dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---</span>] <br id=\"al5-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">5</span><span data-text=\"τύχης\">τύχης</span> Ν[<span dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---</span>] <br id=\"al6-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">6</span>ΟΣ̣ <span data-text=\"πεπ\">πεπ[<span dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---</span>]</span>  </span></div>  <p class=\"miniapp\"></p></div><div class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Jonathan Prag</div><div id=\"edition-diplomatic\" lang=\"grc\"><div class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\"><span class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\"><a id=\"al1-diplomatic\"><!--0--></a><span class=\"linenumber\">1</span><span data-text=\"Θεοῖς\">Θ</span><span data-text=\"Καταχθονίοις\">Κ</span><br id=\"al2-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">2</span><span data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Δάφνη\"><span data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Δάφνη\">ΔΑΦΝΗ</span></span><span data-text=\"γλυκυ\n                    τάτη\">ΓΛΥ[..]<br id=\"al3-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">3</span>ΤΑΤΗ</span><span data-text=\"χαῖρε\">ΧΑΙΡ[.</span><span data-text=\"ἔζη\n                    σας\">...]<br id=\"al4-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">4</span>ΣΑΣ</span><span data-text=\"ἔτη\">ΕΤΗ</span>[<span dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---</span>]<br id=\"al5-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">5</span><span data-text=\"τύχης\">ΤΥΧΗΣ</span>Ν[<span dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---</span>]<br id=\"al6-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">6</span>Ο.<span data-text=\"πεπ\">ΠΕΠ[<span dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---</span>]</span></span></div><p class=\"miniapp\"></p></div></div>  <div id=\"facsimile-images\"><h2>Facsimile Images</h2></div>  <div id=\"apparatus\"><h4>Apparatus criticus</h4><ul><li><span><span>Text after Alessi and Kaibel</span></span>; </li><li><span class=\"line 2\">line.2: <span>Alessi: ΓΛΥΚυ... and ΓΛΥκυ...</span></span><br></li><li><span class=\"line 3\">line.3: <span>[ἔζυ]|σας sic Alessi; ἔζη]|σας Franz; χαῖρ[ε ν’ ζή]|σασ’ ἔτη</span></span><br></li><li><span class=\"line 4\">line.4: <span>ἔτη [ὑπό Alessi</span></span><br></li><li><span class=\"line 5\">line.5: <span>N[εοκορύτ]|ος Alessi; Εὐ]|τύχης [πατὴρ ἴδι]|ος Franz</span></span><br></li><li><span class=\"line 6\">line.6: <span>πεπ[ρωμενυς sic Alessi; πεπ[οίηκεν Franz</span></span></li></ul></div>  <div id=\"translation\"><h2>English translation</h2><p class=\"translation-author\"><a href=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5187-5163\">Marta Fogagnolo</a></p>  <p>To the Underworld Gods. Sweetest Daphne, farewell. You lived for … years. … of fortune …</p>  </div>  <div id=\"commentary\"><h2>commentary</h2>  <p>This is an epitaph for a woman named Daphne, preceded by an invocation to the chthonic gods. The deceased is described with an attribute (ll. 2–3 <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">γλυ[κυ]|τάτη</span>) that is quite common, followed by a greeting and the verb ζάω in the second person singular, with a direct address to the deceased made even more effective by the greeting formula. The age has been lost in a lacuna. The final part of the epitaph is very fragmentary: Kaibel suggests lines 5-6 likely to be consolatory epithets (e.g. <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">τύχης ... πεπρωμεν</span>), rather than e.g. name of a male relative responsible for the building of the monument (as Alessi and Franz believed, since the first supplied at ll. 5-6 <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">Ν[εοκορύτ]|ος πεπ[ρωμένυς</span>, the second at ll. 4-6 <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">Εὐ]|τύχης [πατὴρ ἴδι]|ος πεπ[οίηκεν</span>), and notes a suggestion of Willamowitz that the final part might have been in verse (iambic trimeter), and even the whole, if the age were a single syllable (e.g. <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">Δάφνη γλυ[κυ]|τάτη χαῖρ[ε ν´ ζή]|σασ’ ἔτη</span>).</p>  </div>  <div id=\"bibliography\"><h2>bibliography</h2>  <ul><li> Alessi 1833 226 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002538\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002538</a></li><li> Alessi 1833 172 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002540\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002540</a></li><li> Franz 1853 5703 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001250\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001250</a></li><li> Kaibel 1890 <a href=\"https://clio.columbia.edu/catalog/6873760\" target=\"_blank\">469</a>  <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001072\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001072</a></li></ul>  <ul><li></li></ul>  </div>  <div id=\"handnote\"> Line 1    Interlineation line 1 to 2    </div><div id=\"license\"> Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence </div>",
